<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Harhar</h1><p class="st-meta">800 BCE – 716 BCE (approx.) · capital Harhar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Zagros town on the main road into Iran, captured by Sargon II in 716 BCE and refounded as the Assyrian provincial capital Kar-Sharrukin.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Harhar lay in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a>, probably in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kermanshah">Kermanshah</a> region, at a key point on the route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-plateau">Iranian plateau</a>. It appears in Assyrian sources in the 8th century BCE as a fortified town ruled by local lords in the borderland where Median groups were settling.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Almost nothing is known of its own government. Assyrian texts say that the people of Harhar drove out a ruler installed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> and turned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalta">Dalta</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ellipi">Ellipi</a>, prompting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> to intervene. Its value lay in the trade in horses and goods moving along the road between the plateau and the lowlands.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 716 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> took Harhar, settled deportees there and renamed it Kar-Sharrukin, 'Fort <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon</a>', as the capital of a new Assyrian province facing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a>. It remained an Assyrian outpost until Median expansion in the 7th century BCE.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 800 BCE – 716 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:43.78%;width:1.67%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 BCE – 716 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Harhar</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kar-Sharrukin</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-758&amp;focus=harhar" aria-label="Harhar on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6103 1001 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Harhar lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6092 1134h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6423 1257h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6423 1257h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Iran. <a href="/atlas?year=-758&amp;focus=harhar">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

